{
  "text": " Market crash is a simple question, this money is not a cash that is not a cash that is left out of someone's account Market value is lost and most of the people here are confused You have 100 shares and every share is Rs. 1000 That means your total value is like, now if you get a price of Rs. 700, then your value is Rs. 70,000 Now the question is, where is that 30,000 shares? No one has taken 30,000 from your account Just on the price, your share was ready to buy and that price fell That's why when the market crash is called headlines, it has become a 10 lakh crore wipeout That means it has become a 10 lakh crore cash that is not a 10 lakh crore cash Mostly the total valuation of the market has fallen That's why the money in the market crash is not a habit It is just the value of assets And this difference in trading is very important If you want to understand such a simple language, then follow it",
